      "message": "\u003e  Could you point me to where this pattern matching is done?\n\nForgot that this is being done in the companion CL of this topic (aosp/3143014), which uses a filter rather than a prefix based match.\n\nI think `filepath.Join` should be compatible with aosp_arm64-userdebug. I verified that all the .odex files are installed in /system for this product.\n```\n$ lunch aosp_arm64-trunk_staging-userdebug\n$ grep product.*odex out/target/product/generic_arm64/obj/PACKAGING/system_intermediates/file_list.txt\nproduct/app/Browser2/oat/arm64/Browser2.odex\nproduct/app/Calendar/oat/arm64/Calendar.odex\nproduct/app/Camera2/oat/arm64/Camera2.odex\nproduct/app/DeskClock/oat/arm64/DeskClock.odex\nproduct/app/Gallery2/oat/arm64/Gallery2.odex\nproduct/app/LatinIME/oat/arm64/LatinIME.odex\nproduct/app/Music/oat/arm64/Music.odex\nproduct/app/PhotoTable/oat/arm64/PhotoTable.odex\nproduct/app/QuickSearchBox/oat/arm64/QuickSearchBox.odex\nproduct/app/messaging/oat/arm64/messaging.odex\nproduct/app/webview/oat/arm64/webview.odex\nproduct/priv-app/Contacts/oat/arm64/Contacts.odex\nproduct/priv-app/Dialer/oat/arm64/Dialer.odex\nproduct/priv-app/ImsServiceEntitlement/oat/arm64/ImsServiceEntitlement.odex\nproduct/priv-app/SettingsIntelligence/oat/arm64/SettingsIntelligence.odex\n```",
